# ESP-IDF
build/
build-*/
sdkconfig
sdkconfig.old
managed_components/
dependencies.lock

# CMake / native
cmake-build-*/
CMakeUserPresets.json
compile_commands.json
.cache/

# Secrets and keys — never commit these
secure_boot_signing_key*.pem
*_private.pem
*.key
credentials.*
secrets.*

# Measurement output (regenerate, don't version)
measurements/*.raw
*.log

# Editors / OS
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp

# Python bytecode from tools/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# Archives dropped into the working directory to be unpacked.
# The unpacked result belongs in the tree; the archive does not, and one
# already reached a branch through a `git add -A` that meant well.
*.zip
*.tar.gz
*.tgz

# Pages fetched from vendor and distributor sites while researching a part.
# Same failure as the archives above and it happened a second time: a scraped
# Adafruit page reached `main` in #98 through `git add -A` from the repository
# root. What belongs in the tree is the *reading* of a source in
# docs/research/, identified by URL and revision — never the source itself,
# which is somebody else's copyrighted page. Only the two site files at
# docs/404.html and docs/index.html are tracked HTML; anything at the root is
# a stray.
/*.html
/*.htm
/*.pdf

# Private notes — not for publication
EASTER_EGGS.md

# CTest scratch. `ctest` writes Testing/Temporary/ next to the source tree
# whenever it is run from the repository root; none of it describes the project.
#
# **Anchored**, both of these. Without the leading slash gitignore(5) matches the
# name at any depth, so a vendored `components/*/Testing/` or a future
# `docs/hardware/artifacts/` would vanish from `git add -A` -- this hunk's own
# failure mode, inverted. `Testing/` unanchored is worse than that on a
# case-insensitive checkout, where it also swallows `docs/testing/` -- and that
# is not a hypothetical directory. #121 puts `docs/testing/WATCH_CONTROL.md` in
# it, the file `CLAUDE.md` sends every agent to for the screenshot loop, and
# `docs/` is what the unattended merge sweep is allowed to touch. An unanchored
# line would make it untrackable and a docs-only change would stop carrying it,
# silently. This is written here rather than in a pull request body because a
# squash merge keeps the file and discards the body.
/Testing/

# Screenshots and scenario output from the UI test tooling: evidence for a
# session, not source. They are regenerated by re-running whatever wrote them,
# and a megabyte of PNG per commit is what this line is for. (The tool itself
# arrives with #121; this entry is deliberately written not to depend on it,
# because a rule that cites a file the reader cannot open is unverifiable.)
/artifacts/
